>Check your helmet -- you may be wearing a helm of opposite alignment ...

Also note that Priests start out with a variable alignment -- in 3.1.*
they can start off as lawful, neutral, or chaotic.  Are you sure you 
didn't just start out lawful?

If you don't like being lawful, it is possible to change alignment.  The
two normal ways are wearing a helm of opposite alignment, or sacrificing
on another god's altar.

You see, when you sacrifice on another god's altar, you have a may 
convert the altar to your alignment or convert your alignment to the
altars.  It depends on how high your alignment is.  A sure way of 
lowering your alignment is to kill a unicorn of your alignment.
So, a sure way for your lawful character to become neutral is to
kill a white unicorn, and sacrifice it on a neutral altar.

